		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4626&amp;p=34406#p34406"><![CDATA[
Yes, an accurate counter would work OK. <br><br>The problem is due to the poor receiver performance in most hotspots. They cannot cope well with even small frequency errors and have to be fine tuned to match the radio in use.  Hence if more than one radio is used they all need to be very closely matched to each other in frequency. <br><br>A proper commercial repeater (or a hotspot built with an OpenGD77 radio) does not have this problem and has a much better tolerance to the normal small frequency errors between different radios.  <br><br>Colin G4EML<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Thu Dec 05, 2024 5:40 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
